{
 "events": [
  {
   "text": "The First Air Group was active in various formations.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "from 1938",
   "date": "1938",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "The First Air Group was active in various formations until 1995.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "to 1995",
   "date": "1995",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Swedish Air Force switched from army-like to navy-like naming of its flying units.",
   "chunk": 1,
   "date_text": "In 1936",
   "date": "1936",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#1"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Second Air Corps became the Second Royal Roslagen Flying Flotilla.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": "in 1936",
   "date": "1936",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Swedish Air Force formed an air squadron (Flygeskadern).",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": "In the end of 1938",
   "date": "1938",
   "approximate": true,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [
    "approximate_date"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "It became the First Air Squadron (E1 Första Flygeskadern).",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": "In 1942",
   "date": "1942",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Second and Third followed.",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": "in 1943",
   "date": "1943",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Fourth followed.",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": "in 1945",
   "date": "1945",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Flygeskadern (the Air Group) was organized in response to the emergency preparedness.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "September 1939",
   "date": "1939-09",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "Flygeskadern was resolved (except for the staff) in the latter part of 1940.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "1940",
   "date": "1940",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [
    "date_text_not_in_chunk",
    "derived_date"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its staff was located in Karlsborg.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "from 1939",
   "date": "1939",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its staff was located in Karlsborg until 1942.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "to 1942",
   "date": "1942",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Swedish Air Force expanded its war organization into four air groups and the Air Group was renamed First Air Group (Första flygeskadern, E 1), with its staff in Stockholm.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "In 1942",
   "date": "1942",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "The distribution of the Swedish Air Force wings to the air groups varied from 1 July 1945.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "1 July 1945",
   "date": "1945-07-01",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "The staff were merged with the staff of the Western Airbase Area (Västra flygbasområdet, Flybo V) and was placed in Gothenburg.",
   "chunk": 7,
   "date_text": "1 October 1957",
   "date": "1957-10-01",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#7"
  },
  {
   "text": "The First Air Group became the only air group in the Swedish Air Force, when the three others were decommissioned.",
   "chunk": 7,
   "date_text": "In 1966",
   "date": "1966",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#7"
  },
  {
   "text": "The First Air Group was renamed Attackeskadern (Attack Group) and was led by a joint staff based in Gothenburg until it was decommissioned in 1995.",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "1995",
   "date": "1995",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "The decommissioning decision came in conjunction with the Defence Act of 1992.",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "1992",
   "date": "1992",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was decided that three geographic air commands were to be established on 1 July 1993 and subsequently retrieved the duties from the First Air Group.",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "1 July 1993",
   "date": "1993-07-01",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "The traditions and history of the First Air Group were transferred to the Chief of Air Force Staff, which handed them over to the Air Force Center.",
   "chunk": 9,
   "date_text": "30 June 1998",
   "date": "1998-06-30",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#9"
  },
  {
   "text": "The commander had the rank of colonel.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "Between 1938 and 1941",
   "date": "1938",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "The commander had the rank of colonel.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "1994 to 1995",
   "date": "1994",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "The commander had the rank of major general.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "Between 1941 and 1994",
   "date": "1941",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/First_Air_Group#10"
  },
